1.0 Competition Description and Objective
The objective of the Consulting Engineering Competition is to challenge competitors to design a detailed solution to a large-scale engineering problem. Engineers often perform consulting services for a wide range of problems such as system implementation, company restructuring, production optimization and general design. Competitors must form a proposal that promotes a solution to the “client” (the judges) showing resourcefulness while acting in good faith with the spirit of the competition.
Participants are encouraged to follow the scoring provided. Winning entries will combine originality, (technical and economic) feasibility, business, environmental and ethical implementations, justifiable design choices, and a high-quality presentation.
1.1 Team Composition and Eligibility


Eligibility: All FOUR competitors must be enrolled in a York Undergraduate Engineering Program. All competitors and teams must also meet the requirements outlined by the Lassonde Engineering Society. 
