During this period the competitors will have the opportunity to get to know one another, after which they will begin the first stage of the competition, this stage consisting of thinking and carrying out brainstorming on the engineering problem in question. The teams will start off with a short icebreaker activity lasting 15 minutes in order to define their team roles. They will then use the rest of the time to analyse the constraints, research the relevant background concepts, draw up preliminary designs and prepare their initial system architecture, while the Team Leads will keep an eye on the progress and provide answers to any rule queries.


